  "Id": 2683,
  "Title": "Faculty to join global expert group on teaching and learning",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Dr Jane Rarieya is the second AKU expert to advise Advance HE",
  "GlobalNews": true,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassDAE3C062266D451E9AAD07B11D97D6F8\"><p><br></p><p>Dr Jane Rarieya, director of teaching and learning at AKU\u2019s Network of Quality, Teaching and Learning (QTL_net),&#160;has been appointed to Advance HE\u2019s Expert Advisory Group on Fellowship and Accreditation.</p><div>Advance HE works with higher education institutions around the world to promote excellence in teaching and learning. Dr Rarieya will help shape Advance HE body\u2019s policy and processes with a view of enhancing the professional development of all those who teach and support learning in the sector.</div><div><br></div><div>Dr Rarieya is the second AKU faculty member to provide guidance and expertise to Advance HE. In 2020, Professor Tashmin Khamis, vice-provost Quality,&#160;Teaching and Learning, was appointed to Advance HE's Global Perspectives Strategic Advisory Group which works in consultation with members to shape the future direction of the organisation.</div><div><br></div><div>In 2019, AKU became the first University in South Asia and East Africa to gain accreditation by Advance HE (UK).&#160;All universities in the UK are subscribers to Advance HE which has strategic partnerships with Higher Education Institutions in 23 other countries.&#160;</div><div>\u200b<br><br></div></div>",
